msgstr "下列提升方法为保持源码兼容而保留。它们不出现在接口文件中，从其他包调用时会产生警告。"

#: manual/api/elab.md:405
msgid "Method"
msgstr "方法"

#: manual/api/elab.md:405
msgid "Replacement"
msgstr "替代"

#: manual/api/elab.md:408
msgid "`Repr(x)`, `@debug.to_string(x)` or `debug_inspect(x)`"
msgstr "`Repr(x)`、`@debug.to_string(x)` 或 `debug_inspect(x)`"

#: manual/api/elab.md:410
msgid "Before the MoonBit 0.10 migration, `Name`, `TermChk`, `TermInf`, `Neutral` and `Value` implemented `Show`. These implementations were removed: `inspect(x)`, `x.to_string()` and `\"\\{x}\"` no longer compile for these types. Use the `Debug` forms instead."
msgstr "在迁移到 MoonBit 0.10 之前，`Name`、`TermChk`、`TermInf`、`Neutral` 和 `Value` 实现了 `Show`。这些实现已被移除：对这些类型，`inspect(x)`、`x.to_string()` 和 `\"\\{x}\"` 不再能通过编译。请改用 `Debug` 形式。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:1
msgid "elab design"
msgstr "elab 设计"

#: manual/design/elab.md:3
msgid "The `elab` package is the kernel of stella. It implements a dependent type theory in the style of Martin-Löf with a unit type, $\\Pi$, $\\Sigma$, identity and W types and a cumulative hierarchy of universes, and it decides typing with a bidirectional checker whose definitional equality is computed by normalisation by evaluation (NbE). This page states the rules the code implements, derives the properties that make them work, and records where the implementation is incomplete."
msgstr "`elab` 包是 stella 的内核。它实现了一个 Martin-Löf 风格的依值类型论，包含单位类型、$\\Pi$、$\\Sigma$、恒等类型、W 类型以及累积的宇宙层级；它用双向检查器判定类型，其定义等价由求值归一化（NbE）计算。本页陈述代码实现的规则，推导使这些规则成立的性质，并记录实现尚不完整之处。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:5
msgid "Design goal"
msgstr "设计目标"

#: manual/design/elab.md:7
msgid "A small, readable kernel whose structure mirrors the theory: one function per judgement, one match arm per rule."
msgstr "一个小巧、可读的内核，其结构与理论对应：每个判断一个函数，每条规则一个匹配分支。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:8
msgid "Decidable checking with few annotations: the user annotates only where the checker cannot infer."
msgstr "可判定的检查且只需少量标注：用户只在检查器无法推断的地方添加标注。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:9
msgid "Equality of types by computation: two types are compared by evaluating them and comparing normal forms, not by rewriting syntax."
msgstr "通过计算判定类型相等：比较两个类型时，先对其求值再比较范式，而不是改写语法。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:10
msgid "An implementation close to the references the project follows: Löh, McBride and Swierstra's tutorial implementation $\\lambda\\Pi$ and Norell's thesis on Agda.[^refs]"
msgstr "实现贴近本项目参照的文献：Löh、McBride 和 Swierstra 的教程式实现 $\\lambda\\Pi$，以及 Norell 关于 Agda 的博士论文。[^refs]"

#: manual/design/elab.md:12
msgid "A. Löh, C. McBride, W. Swierstra, \"A tutorial implementation of a dependently typed lambda calculus\", *Fundamenta Informaticae* 102 (2010). U. Norell, *Towards a practical programming language based on dependent type theory*, PhD thesis, Chalmers (2007)."
msgstr "A. Löh, C. McBride, W. Swierstra, \"A tutorial implementation of a dependently typed lambda calculus\", *Fundamenta Informaticae* 102 (2010). U. Norell, *Towards a practical programming language based on dependent type theory*, PhD thesis, Chalmers (2007)."

#: manual/design/elab.md:14
msgid "Constraints"
msgstr "约束"

#: manual/design/elab.md:16
msgid "Terms are MoonBit values built by the user; there is no parser, so the core syntax must be usable directly."
msgstr "项是由用户构造的 MoonBit 值；没有解析器，因此核心语法必须能够直接使用。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:17
msgid "MoonBit closures cannot be compared or printed, so a value that contains a binder can only be inspected by applying it, and every equality test on values has to go through application or read-back."
msgstr "MoonBit 闭包无法比较也无法打印，因此含有绑定子的值只能通过应用来检查，值上的每一次相等性测试都必须经由应用或读回。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:18
msgid "The kernel must stay small enough to audit by reading: each rule is one match arm, and the checker has no unification, no metavariables and no global state."
msgstr "内核必须保持足够小，以便通过阅读来审计：每条规则是一个 match 分支，检查器没有合一、没有元变量，也没有全局状态。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:20
msgid "Mathematical background"
msgstr "数学背景"

#: manual/design/elab.md:24
msgid "Terms are split by the judgement that handles them. Writing $e$ for inferable terms (`TermInf`) and $t$ for checkable terms (`TermChk`):"
msgstr "项按处理它们的判断划分。记 $e$ 为可推断项（`TermInf`），$t$ 为可检查项（`TermChk`）："

#: manual/design/elab.md:34
msgid "Bound variables are de Bruijn indices $\\#i$ (`Bound(i)`): $\\#0$ refers to the nearest enclosing binder. The binders are $\\lambda$ and the second argument of $\\Pi$, $\\Sigma$ and $W$. Because a bound variable has no name, two terms are $\\alpha$-equivalent exactly when they are equal as trees, so the derived `Eq` of `TermInf` and `TermChk` *is* $\\alpha$-equivalence."
msgstr "约束变量是德布鲁因索引 $\\#i$（`Bound(i)`）：$\\#0$ 指最近的外层绑定子。绑定子是 $\\lambda$ 以及 $\\Pi$、$\\Sigma$ 和 $W$ 的第二个参数。由于约束变量没有名字，两个项 $\\alpha$-等价当且仅当它们作为树相等，因此 `TermInf` 和 `TermChk` 派生的 `Eq` *就是* $\\alpha$-等价。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:36
msgid "Values and neutral terms"
msgstr "值与中性项"

#: manual/design/elab.md:38
msgid "Evaluation maps terms into a semantic domain $D$ (`Value`):"
msgstr "求值将项映射到语义域 $D$（`Value`）："

#: manual/design/elab.md:47
msgid "where $f, F : D \\to D$ are MoonBit functions. A binder body becomes a function on values: $\\Pi(A, F)$ is the type $\\Pi_{x : A} F(x)$. The neutral terms $n$ (`Neutral`) are eliminations stuck on a free variable $x$."
msgstr "其中 $f, F : D \\to D$ 是 MoonBit 函数。绑定子的体变成值上的函数：$\\Pi(A, F)$ 是类型 $\\Pi_{x : A} F(x)$。中性项 $n$（`Neutral`）是卡在自由变量 $x$ 上的消去。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:49
msgid "Every value is in weak head normal form: no elimination is applied to an introduction form, because the evaluator reduces such redexes as soon as it builds them. Bodies of binders are not normalised: a closure $F$ is only evaluated when it is applied, by the checker or by read-back."
msgstr "每个值都处于弱头范式：不存在作用于引入形式的消去，因为求值器在构造此类可约式时就立即将其归约。绑定子的体不会被规范化：闭包 $F$ 只有在被应用时才求值，应用者是检查器或读回。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:53
msgid "Evaluation $\\llbracket t \\rrbracket_\\rho$ (`eval_inf`, `eval_chk`) takes an environment $\\rho$ whose $i$-th entry is the value of $\\#i$:"
msgstr "求值 $\\llbracket t \\rrbracket_\\rho$（`eval_inf`、`eval_chk`）接受一个环境 $\\rho$，其第 $i$ 个条目是 $\\#i$ 的值："

#: manual/design/elab.md:66
msgid "and similarly for the other constructors. The semantic eliminations (`val_app`, `val_fst`, `val_snd`, `val_j_elim`, `val_w_rec`) carry the computation rules:"
msgstr "其他构造子类似。语义消去（`val_app`、`val_fst`、`val_snd`、`val_j_elim`、`val_w_rec`）承载计算规则："

#: manual/design/elab.md:77
msgid "and on a neutral argument they extend the spine, for example $\\underline{n} \\cdot v = \\underline{n\\;v}$. Annotations are erased."
msgstr "对中性参数，它们扩展序列，例如 $\\underline{n} \\cdot v = \\underline{n\\;v}$。标注被擦除。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:79
msgid "Read-back and normal forms"
msgstr "读回与范式"

#: manual/design/elab.md:81
msgid "Read-back $q_l$ (`quote`, `neutral_quote`) turns a value under $l$ binders into a term. A function is read back by applying it to a fresh variable:"
msgstr "读回 $q_l$（`quote`、`neutral_quote`）将处于 $l$ 个绑定子之下的值转为项。函数通过应用于新变量来读回："

#: manual/design/elab.md:88
msgid "and a fresh variable is turned back into an index:"
msgstr "而新变量被还原为索引："

#: manual/design/elab.md:94
msgid "*Why $l - k - 1$.* Read-back numbers binders by *level*, from the outside: the binder opened at depth $k$ introduces $\\mathsf{Quote}(k)$. At depth $l$, the binders opened after it have levels $k + 1, \\dots, l - 1$, so $l - 1 - k$ binders lie between the occurrence and its binder, which is its de Bruijn *index*. The variable is fresh because at depth $l$ only $\\mathsf{Quote}(0), \\dots, \\mathsf{Quote}(l-1)$ are in scope. Levels make freshness trivial (no renaming, no shifting), and indices make the output canonical."
msgstr "*为何是 $l - k - 1$。* 读回按*层级*从外向内为绑定子编号：在深度 $k$ 打开的绑定子引入 $\\mathsf{Quote}(k)$。在深度 $l$ 处，在它之后打开的绑定子层级为 $k + 1, \\dots, l - 1$，因此该出现与其绑定子之间隔着 $l - 1 - k$ 个绑定子，这正是它的德布鲁因*索引*。该变量是新的，因为在深度 $l$ 处只有 $\\mathsf{Quote}(0), \\dots, \\mathsf{Quote}(l-1)$ 在作用域内。层级使新鲜性变得平凡（无需重命名、无需移位），而索引使输出规范。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:96
msgid "The *normal form* of a closed term is $\\mathrm{nf}(t) = q_0(\\llbracket t \\rrbracket_\\varepsilon)$."
msgstr "闭项的*范式*为 $\\mathrm{nf}(t) = q_0(\\llbracket t \\rrbracket_\\varepsilon)$。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:98
msgid "Why evaluation respects $\\beta$"
msgstr "为何求值遵守 $\\beta$"

#: manual/design/elab.md:100
msgid "Write $t \\to u$ for one step of the reduction the evaluator implements: a $\\beta$-step $(\\lambda.\\,t : T)\\;u \\to t[u]$, a projection of a pair, $J$ on $\\mathrm{refl}$, $\\mathrm{wrec}$ on $\\sup$, or the erasure $(t : T) \\to t$ of an annotation, at any position in the term. With de Bruijn indices, $t[u]$ replaces $\\#0$ by $u$ and lowers every other free index of $t$ by one, because the binder that $\\#0$ referred to is gone."
msgstr "记 $t \\to u$ 为求值器所实现的归约的一步：$\\beta$ 步 $(\\lambda.\\,t : T)\\;u \\to t[u]$、对的投影、$J$ 作用于 $\\mathrm{refl}$、$\\mathrm{wrec}$ 作用于 $\\sup$，或者标注的擦除 $(t : T) \\to t$，可发生在项中的任意位置。使用 de Bruijn 索引时，$t[u]$ 把 $\\#0$ 替换为 $u$，并把 $t$ 的其他自由索引减一，因为 $\\#0$ 所指的绑定子已经消失。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:102
msgid "Values contain closures, so \"the same value\" means the same read-back: $v \\simeq w$ when $q_l(v) = q_l(w)$ at every level $l$ and for every way of applying them. The central lemma of NbE is that a reduction step does not change the value. For a redex,"
msgstr "值包含闭包，因此“同一个值”指读回相同：当 $q_l(v) = q_l(w)$ 在每个层级 $l$ 上、对每种应用方式都成立时，记 $v \\simeq w$。NbE 的核心引理是：一步归约不改变值。对一个可约式，"

#: manual/design/elab.md:118
msgid "The substitution lemma $\\llbracket t \\rrbracket_{\\llbracket u \\rrbracket_\\rho :: \\rho} = \\llbracket t[u] \\rrbracket_\\rho$ is proved by induction on $t$. Going under binders forces a more general statement: for an environment prefix $\\sigma$ of length $k$,"
msgstr "替换引理 $\\llbracket t \\rrbracket_{\\llbracket u \\rrbracket_\\rho :: \\rho} = \\llbracket t[u] \\rrbracket_\\rho$ 通过对 $t$ 归纳证明。进入绑定子时需要更一般的陈述：对长度为 $k$ 的环境前缀 $\\sigma$，"

#: manual/design/elab.md:124
msgid "where $t[k \\mapsto u]$ replaces $\\#k$ by $u$ with its free indices raised by $k$, and lowers the indices above $k$ by one. An occurrence of $\\#k$ evaluates to $\\llbracket u \\rrbracket_\\rho$ on the left, and on the right to the raised copy of $u$ in $\\sigma \\mathbin{+\\!\\!+} \\rho$, which skips the $k$ entries of $\\sigma$ and therefore also evaluates to $\\llbracket u \\rrbracket_\\rho$. An index below $k$ is bound inside $t$ and reads the same entry of $\\sigma$ on both sides. An index above $k$ reads one position further on the left, which is what the lowering compensates. Every other constructor follows from the induction hypothesis, with $k + 1$ under a binder. The other redexes reduce by the computation rules $\\Sigma\\beta$, $J\\beta$ and $W\\beta$ of `val_fst`, `val_snd`, `val_j_elim` and `val_w_rec`, and evaluation is compositional, so a step inside a subterm changes only the value of that subterm. Hence"
msgstr "其中 $t[k \\mapsto u]$ 把 $\\#k$ 替换为自由索引上移 $k$ 的 $u$，并把大于 $k$ 的索引减一。$\\#k$ 的出现在左边求值为 $\\llbracket u \\rrbracket_\\rho$；在右边则是上移后的 $u$ 在 $\\sigma \\mathbin{+\\!\\!+} \\rho$ 中求值，它跳过 $\\sigma$ 的 $k$ 个条目，因此同样求值为 $\\llbracket u \\rrbracket_\\rho$。小于 $k$ 的索引在 $t$ 内部被绑定，两边读取 $\\sigma$ 的同一条目。大于 $k$ 的索引在左边多读一个位置，这正由减一来补偿。其他构造子都由归纳假设得到，进入绑定子时用 $k + 1$。其他可约式由 `val_fst`、`val_snd`、`val_j_elim` 和 `val_w_rec` 的计算规则 $\\Sigma\\beta$、$J\\beta$ 和 $W\\beta$ 归约；求值是组合式的，因此子项内的一步只改变该子项的值。于是"

#: manual/design/elab.md:130
msgid "and since $\\simeq$ is an equivalence, terms that are equal under the symmetric closure $=_\\beta$ of $\\to$ have equal normal forms. Conversely, $\\mathrm{nf}(t)$ is reached from $t$ by reduction steps, because every equation of $\\llbracket - \\rrbracket$ and $q_l$ either rebuilds a constructor or performs one of the steps above; so equal normal forms imply $t =_\\beta \\mathrm{nf}(t) = \\mathrm{nf}(u) =_\\beta u$. Together these make \"compare normal forms\" a decision procedure for $=_\\beta$ on terms whose evaluation terminates without a panic, which includes every well-typed closed term.[^nbe]"
msgstr "又因为 $\\simeq$ 是等价关系，在 $\\to$ 的对称闭包 $=_\\beta$ 下相等的项具有相同的范式。反过来，$\\mathrm{nf}(t)$ 可由 $t$ 经归约步得到，因为 $\\llbracket - \\rrbracket$ 和 $q_l$ 的每个方程要么重建一个构造子，要么执行上述某一步；因此范式相等蕴含 $t =_\\beta \\mathrm{nf}(t) = \\mathrm{nf}(u) =_\\beta u$。两者合起来，使“比较范式”成为在求值终止且不 panic 的项上判定 $=_\\beta$ 的过程，这包括所有良类型的闭项。[^nbe]"

#: manual/design/elab.md:132
msgid "Read-back is untyped, so it does not $\\eta$-expand: `quote` keeps a variable $f$ of type $\\mathbf 1 \\to \\mathbf 1$ as $f$, while $\\lambda x.\\,f\\,x$ reads back as a $\\lambda$. The checker adds $\\eta$ in the type-directed conversion below; normal forms from `quote` decide $\\beta$ only."
msgstr "读回是无类型的，因此不做 $\\eta$-展开：`quote` 把类型为 $\\mathbf 1 \\to \\mathbf 1$ 的变量 $f$ 保持为 $f$，而 $\\lambda x.\\,f\\,x$ 读回为一个 $\\lambda$。检查器在下面的类型导向转换中加入 $\\eta$；`quote` 给出的范式只判定 $\\beta$。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:134
msgid "U. Berger and H. Schwichtenberg, \"An inverse of the evaluation functional for typed λ-calculus\", LICS 1991, introduced NbE. A. Abel, *Normalization by Evaluation: Dependent Types and Impredicativity*, habilitation, LMU Munich (2013), proves soundness and completeness of NbE for Martin-Löf type theory with $\\eta$. These are results about the theory; for this implementation they are tested, not proved."
msgstr "U. Berger 和 H. Schwichtenberg 的“An inverse of the evaluation functional for typed λ-calculus”（LICS 1991）提出了 NbE。A. Abel 的 *Normalization by Evaluation: Dependent Types and Impredicativity*（教授资格论文，LMU Munich，2013）证明了 NbE 对带 $\\eta$ 的 Martin-Löf 类型论的可靠性与完备性。这些是关于理论的结果；对于本实现，它们只经过测试，而未被证明。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:136
msgid "The bidirectional judgements"
msgstr "双向判断"

#: manual/design/elab.md:138
msgid "The checker has two judgements, each a function:"
msgstr "检查器有两个判断，各对应一个函数："

#: manual/design/elab.md:140
msgid "$\\Gamma; \\rho \\vdash_l e \\Rightarrow A$ (*inference*, `type_inf`): $e$ has type $A$, which the checker computes;"
msgstr "$\\Gamma; \\rho \\vdash_l e \\Rightarrow A$（*推断*，`type_inf`）：$e$ 的类型为 $A$，由检查器计算得出；"

#: manual/design/elab.md:141
msgid "$\\Gamma; \\rho \\vdash_l t \\Leftarrow A$ (*checking*, `type_chk`): $t$ has the given type $A$."
msgstr "$\\Gamma; \\rho \\vdash_l t \\Leftarrow A$（*检查*，`type_chk`）：$t$ 具有给定类型 $A$。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:143
msgid "The context $\\Gamma$ maps names to types (values), $\\rho$ is the environment of the current position, and $l$ counts the binders entered. Under a binder the checker extends all three with a fresh variable $x_l = \\underline{\\mathsf{Local}(l)}$: it writes $\\Gamma, x_l : A;\\ \\rho, x_l \\vdash_{l+1}$. Thus $\\rho$ always maps $\\#i$ to the variable $x_{l-1-i}$, and $\\Gamma$ gives its type. Below, $\\llbracket t \\rrbracket$ abbreviates $\\llbracket t \\rrbracket_\\rho$."
msgstr "上下文 $\\Gamma$ 将名字映射到类型（值），$\\rho$ 是当前位置的环境，$l$ 计数已进入的绑定子。在绑定子之下，检查器用新变量 $x_l = \\underline{\\mathsf{Local}(l)}$ 同时扩展这三者：记作 $\\Gamma, x_l : A;\\ \\rho, x_l \\vdash_{l+1}$。因此 $\\rho$ 总是将 $\\#i$ 映射为变量 $x_{l-1-i}$，而 $\\Gamma$ 给出其类型。下文中 $\\llbracket t \\rrbracket$ 是 $\\llbracket t \\rrbracket_\\rho$ 的简写。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:145
msgid "**Variables, constants and annotations.**"
msgstr "**变量、常量与标注。**"

#: manual/design/elab.md:155
msgid "**Universes and type formers.** Here and below, a premise $T \\Rightarrow \\mathcal U_i$ requires $T$ to be an inferable term whose inferred type *is* a universe; there is no subsumption in these premises."
msgstr "**宇宙与类型构造子。** 此处及下文中，前提 $T \\Rightarrow \\mathcal U_i$ 要求 $T$ 是可推断项且其推断类型*就是*一个宇宙；这些前提中不存在包含（subsumption）。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:165
msgid "The rules $(\\Sigma\\textsf{-F})$ and $(W\\textsf{-F})$ are the same with $\\Sigma$ and $W$ in place of $\\Pi$. The identity type lives in the universe of its carrier:"
msgstr "规则 $(\\Sigma\\textsf{-F})$ 和 $(W\\textsf{-F})$ 与之相同，只是将 $\\Pi$ 换成 $\\Sigma$ 和 $W$。恒等类型位于其载体所在的宇宙中："

#: manual/design/elab.md:171
msgid "**Introductions are checked.** The expected type supplies what the term omits, such as the domain of a $\\lambda$:"
msgstr "**引入形式需检查。** 期望类型提供项所省略的信息，例如 $\\lambda$ 的定义域："

#: manual/design/elab.md:187
msgid "**Eliminations are inferred.** The type of the eliminated term is inferred and then taken apart:"
msgstr "**消去形式需推断。** 先推断被消去项的类型，再将其拆解："

#: manual/design/elab.md:197
msgid "Path induction, with the motive $P$ inferred and $\\bar A = \\llbracket A \\rrbracket$, $\\bar x = \\llbracket x \\rrbracket$, $\\bar y = \\llbracket y \\rrbracket$, $\\bar P = \\llbracket P \\rrbracket$:"
msgstr "路径归纳，其中动机 $P$ 被推断，且 $\\bar A = \\llbracket A \\rrbracket$、$\\bar x = \\llbracket x \\rrbracket$、$\\bar y = \\llbracket y \\rrbracket$、$\\bar P = \\llbracket P \\rrbracket$："

#: manual/design/elab.md:216
msgid "The universe level $k$ of the motive is inferred rather than fixed, which is what cumulative universes need. The two domains are still checked: $P$ is only ever applied to a point of $\\bar A$ and to a path out of $\\bar x$, so its domains must accept those arguments, and $\\Pi$ is contravariant in its domain. Checking only the shape $\\Pi(D_1, \\Pi(D_2, \\mathcal U_k))$ would let $P$ be applied to arguments of the wrong type during checking."
msgstr "motive 的宇宙层级 $k$ 是推断出来的，而不是固定的，这正是累积宇宙所需要的。但两个定义域仍然要检查：$P$ 只会被应用到 $\\bar A$ 中的点以及从 $\\bar x$ 出发的路径上，因此它的定义域必须接受这些参数，而 $\\Pi$ 在定义域上是逆变的。如果只检查形状 $\\Pi(D_1, \\Pi(D_2, \\mathcal U_k))$，检查过程中 $P$ 就可能被应用到类型错误的参数上。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:218
msgid "W recursion, where $B$ is an inferable *function* $A \\to \\mathcal U_k$, $\\bar B(v) = \\llbracket B \\rrbracket \\cdot v$ and $\\bar W = W(\\bar A, \\bar B)$:"
msgstr "W 递归，其中 $B$ 是可推断的*函数* $A \\to \\mathcal U_k$，$\\bar B(v) = \\llbracket B \\rrbracket \\cdot v$，$\\bar W = W(\\bar A, \\bar B)$："

#: manual/design/elab.md:232
msgid "**Changing direction.** An inferable term is accepted in checking mode when its type is a subtype of the expected one:"
msgstr "**切换方向。** 当可推断项的类型是期望类型的子类型时，它在检查模式下被接受："

#: manual/design/elab.md:238
msgid "The opposite direction is $(\\textsf{Ann})$: a checkable term becomes inferable once its type is written down."
msgstr "相反方向是 $(\\textsf{Ann})$：可检查项一旦写下其类型，就成为可推断的。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:240
msgid "Subtyping and conversion"
msgstr "子类型与转换"

#: manual/design/elab.md:242
msgid "The relation $A \\le A'$ (`subtype_nf`, exposed for the empty context as `def_eq`) is cumulativity:"
msgstr "关系 $A \\le A'$（`subtype_nf`，在空上下文中以 `def_eq` 对外提供）即累积性："

#: manual/design/elab.md:254
msgid "The $\\Pi$ rule is contravariant in the domain: a function that accepts every element of $A$ accepts every element of a subtype $A' \\le A$, and its results in $F(x)$ are also results in the supertype $F'(x)$. The $\\Sigma$ rule keeps the first component *invariant*; covariance would also be sound, but the implementation, and its tests, require conversion there."
msgstr "$\\Pi$ 规则在定义域上逆变：接受 $A$ 中每个元素的函数，也接受子类型 $A' \\le A$ 中的每个元素，而其在 $F(x)$ 中的结果也是超类型 $F'(x)$ 中的结果。$\\Sigma$ 规则保持第一分量*不变*；协变同样是可靠的，但实现及其测试要求此处使用转换。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:256
msgid "Conversion $A \\equiv A'$ (`conv_type`) compares types structurally, entering binders with a fresh variable, and compares the endpoints of identity types with the type-directed $\\equiv_A$ (`conv_nf`), which adds $\\eta$:"
msgstr "转换 $A \\equiv A'$（`conv_type`）按结构比较类型，用新变量进入绑定子，并用类型导向的 $\\equiv_A$（`conv_nf`）比较恒等类型的端点，后者加入了 $\\eta$："

#: manual/design/elab.md:264
msgid "Neutral terms are compared spine by spine (`conv_neu`), looking up the type of the head variable in $\\Gamma$ to compare application arguments at the right type. When the head's type is not in $\\Gamma$, as in `def_eq`, which has no context, the two spines are compared by their read-backs instead. That is sound, because equal read-backs are definitionally equal, but it does not use $\\eta$ on the arguments. Everything else falls back to comparing read-backs, $q_l(v) = q_l(v')$."
msgstr "中性项逐个序列比较（`conv_neu`），在 $\\Gamma$ 中查找头部变量的类型，以便在正确的类型下比较应用参数。当头部的类型不在 $\\Gamma$ 中时（例如没有上下文的 `def_eq`），两个序列改为按读回结果比较。这是可靠的，因为读回结果相同的值在定义上相等，但它不会对参数使用 $\\eta$。其他所有情况退化为比较读回结果 $q_l(v) = q_l(v')$。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:266
msgid "Universes"
msgstr "宇宙"

#: manual/design/elab.md:268
msgid "The universes are *predicative* and *Russell style*: a type is itself a term, and $\\mathcal U_i : \\mathcal U_{i+1}$. There is no rule $\\mathcal U_i : \\mathcal U_i$, because a universe containing itself makes the theory inconsistent (Girard's paradox).[^girard] A type former lands in the larger universe of its parts, $\\max(i, j)$, which is what predicativity requires: $\\Pi_{A : \\mathcal U_0} A \\to A$ quantifies over $\\mathcal U_0$ and therefore lives in $\\mathcal U_1$. Cumulativity $\\mathcal U_i \\le \\mathcal U_{i+1}$ is not a typing rule but part of subtyping, used by $(\\textsf{Sub})$."
msgstr "宇宙是*直谓的*、*Russell 风格*的：类型本身就是项，且 $\\mathcal U_i : \\mathcal U_{i+1}$。不存在规则 $\\mathcal U_i : \\mathcal U_i$，因为包含自身的宇宙会使理论不一致（Girard 悖论）。[^girard] 类型构造子落在其各部分中较大的宇宙 $\\max(i, j)$ 中，这正是直谓性的要求：$\\Pi_{A : \\mathcal U_0} A \\to A$ 对 $\\mathcal U_0$ 进行量化，因而位于 $\\mathcal U_1$ 中。累积性 $\\mathcal U_i \\le \\mathcal U_{i+1}$ 不是类型规则，而是子类型关系的一部分，由 $(\\textsf{Sub})$ 使用。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:270
msgid "J.-Y. Girard, *Interprétation fonctionnelle et élimination des coupures de l'arithmétique d'ordre supérieur*, thèse d'État (1972); a short proof is A. J. C. Hurkens, \"A simplification of Girard's paradox\", TLCA 1995."
msgstr "J.-Y. Girard, *Interprétation fonctionnelle et élimination des coupures de l'arithmétique d'ordre supérieur*, thèse d'État (1972)；简短的证明见 A. J. C. Hurkens, \"A simplification of Girard's paradox\", TLCA 1995。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:272
msgid "Design decisions"
msgstr "设计决策"

#: manual/design/elab.md:274
msgid "Bidirectional checking"
msgstr "双向检查"

#: manual/design/elab.md:276
msgid "**Problem.** Inferring the type of an unannotated $\\lambda$ in a dependent type theory requires guessing its domain, which in general means higher-order unification, which is undecidable."
msgstr "**问题。** 在依值类型论中推断未标注 $\\lambda$ 的类型需要猜测其定义域，一般而言这意味着高阶合一，而高阶合一是不可判定的。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:278
msgid "**Options.** (a) Annotate every binder, $\\lambda (x : A).\\,t$. (b) Infer with unification variables. (c) Split the terms into checked and inferred ones."
msgstr "**选项。** (a) 标注每个绑定子，$\\lambda (x : A).\\,t$。(b) 用合一变量进行推断。(c) 将项划分为需检查的和可推断的两类。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:280
msgid "**Choice.** (c). Introduction forms ($\\lambda$, pairs, $\\star$, $\\mathrm{refl}$, $\\sup$) are checked, because their type determines the missing information; eliminations and type formers are inferred, because the type of the head determines the type of the whole. An annotation is needed only where an introduction meets an elimination, that is, at a $\\beta$-redex such as $(\\lambda.\\,t : T)\\;u$, or where a function must be inferable: the motives of $J$ and $\\mathrm{wrec}$ and the family $B$ of $\\mathrm{wrec}$. A term in normal form checked against a known type needs no other annotations. Encoding the split in the types `TermInf` and `TermChk` makes an unannotated redex unrepresentable rather than a runtime error."
msgstr "**选择。** (c)。引入形式（$\\lambda$、对、$\\star$、$\\mathrm{refl}$、$\\sup$）需检查，因为其类型决定了缺失的信息；消去形式和类型构造子可推断，因为头部的类型决定了整体的类型。只有在引入形式遇到消去形式时才需要标注，即在 $(\\lambda.\\,t : T)\\;u$ 这样的 $\\beta$-可约式处，或在函数必须可推断的地方：$J$ 和 $\\mathrm{wrec}$ 的动机，以及 $\\mathrm{wrec}$ 的族 $B$。对照已知类型检查的范式项不需要其他标注。将这种划分编码进类型 `TermInf` 和 `TermChk`，使得未标注的可约式无法表示，而不是成为运行时错误。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:282
msgid "Values with closures"
msgstr "带闭包的值"

#: manual/design/elab.md:284
msgid "**Problem.** Comparing types requires evaluating them, including under binders."
msgstr "**问题。** 比较类型需要对其求值，包括在绑定子之下。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:286
msgid "**Options.** (a) Rewrite syntax by substitution, which needs capture-avoiding substitution and index shifting at every step. (b) Evaluate into a semantic domain where binders are host functions."
msgstr "**选项。** (a) 通过代换改写语法，这需要在每一步做避免捕获的代换和索引移位。(b) 求值到一个语义域，其中绑定子是宿主语言的函数。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:288
msgid "**Choice.** (b). A body is represented by a MoonBit function `(Value) -> Value`, so $\\beta$-reduction is a host function call and substitution never happens on syntax. Read-back recovers syntax only when needed: for printing, for comparison by $q_l$, and in the checks that compare normal forms."
msgstr "**选择。** (b)。函数体由 MoonBit 函数 `(Value) -> Value` 表示，因此 $\\beta$-归约是一次宿主函数调用，代换从不发生在语法上。读回只在需要时恢复语法：用于打印、用于以 $q_l$ 进行比较，以及用于比较范式的检查中。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:290
msgid "Indices in terms, levels in values"
msgstr "项中用索引，值中用层级"

#: manual/design/elab.md:292
msgid "Terms use indices, so that $\\alpha$-equivalence is structural equality and closed subterms do not depend on their position. Fresh variables in values use levels, `Local(l)` for the checker and `Quote(l)` for read-back, so that creating a fresh variable is a counter increment and values never need shifting. The two kinds of fresh variable are separate `Name` constructors, so a variable introduced by the checker cannot be mistaken for one introduced while reading back."
msgstr "项使用索引，使得 $\\alpha$-等价就是结构相等，且闭子项不依赖于其位置。值中的新变量使用层级——检查器用 `Local(l)`，读回用 `Quote(l)`——使得创建新变量只是计数器加一，值永远不需要移位。两种新变量是不同的 `Name` 构造子，因此检查器引入的变量不会与读回时引入的变量混淆。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:294
msgid "Subtyping instead of explicit lifts"
msgstr "以子类型代替显式提升"

#: manual/design/elab.md:296
msgid "Cumulativity could be expressed with explicit lifting operators $\\uparrow : \\mathcal U_i \\to \\mathcal U_{i+1}$. Building it into the change of direction $(\\textsf{Sub})$ instead means a type written in $\\mathcal U_0$ can be used in $\\mathcal U_1$ without any term-level coercion, as in `type_chk(..., Inf(UnitType), VUniverse(1))`."
msgstr "累积性可以用显式提升算子 $\\uparrow : \\mathcal U_i \\to \\mathcal U_{i+1}$ 表达。改为将其内置于方向切换 $(\\textsf{Sub})$ 中，意味着写在 $\\mathcal U_0$ 中的类型可以在 $\\mathcal U_1$ 中使用，无需任何项层面的强制转换，如 `type_chk(..., Inf(UnitType), VUniverse(1))`。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:298
msgid "Correctness and invariants"
msgstr "正确性与不变式"

#: manual/design/elab.md:300
msgid "**Environment invariant.** At level $l$, `env` has exactly $l$ entries, entry $i$ is $x_{l-1-i}$, and `ctx` declares every $x_k$. The rules that go under a binder are the only places that extend the state, and they extend all three together. $(\\textsf{Var})$ relies on this invariant. A caller of `type_inf` that breaks it gets `Internal error: Bound variable not in environment` when entry $i$ is not a variable, `Unknown Identifier` when the variable is missing from `ctx`, and a panic when `env` has no entry $i$ (see the known gaps)."
msgstr "**环境不变式。** 在层级 $l$ 处，`env` 恰有 $l$ 个条目，第 $i$ 个条目为 $x_{l-1-i}$，且 `ctx` 声明了每个 $x_k$。进入绑定子的规则是唯一扩展状态的地方，并且它们同时扩展这三者。$(\\textsf{Var})$ 依赖于这一不变式。破坏它的 `type_inf` 调用者：当第 $i$ 个条目不是变量时得到 `Internal error: Bound variable not in environment`，当变量不在 `ctx` 中时得到 `Unknown Identifier`，当 `env` 没有第 $i$ 个条目时则 panic（见已知缺口）。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:301
msgid "**Evaluate only what has been checked.** In every rule, a subterm is evaluated after the premise that checks it, for example the argument in $(\\Pi\\textsf{-E})$ and the type in $(\\textsf{Ann})$. Since the evaluator panics on ill-typed redexes, this ordering is what keeps the checker total on ill-typed input: it raises `TypeError` before it evaluates."
msgstr "**只对已检查的内容求值。** 在每条规则中，子项都在检查它的前提之后才被求值，例如 $(\\Pi\\textsf{-E})$ 中的参数和 $(\\textsf{Ann})$ 中的类型。由于求值器在类型错误的可约式上会 panic，正是这种顺序使检查器在类型错误的输入上保持全函数：它会在求值之前抛出 `TypeError`。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:302
msgid "**Stability of types.** Every type the checker returns is a value, so the caller never has to normalise it again, and every comparison of types happens on values."
msgstr "**类型的稳定性。** 检查器返回的每个类型都是值，因此调用者无需再次归一化，所有类型比较都在值上进行。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:303
msgid "**Termination.** Evaluation of a well-typed term terminates by the normalisation theorem for Martin-Löf type theory with W types and predicative universes. The checker only evaluates terms that it has already checked (invariant 2), and every recursive call of `type_inf` and `type_chk` is on a proper subterm, so the checker terminates on every input as long as the rules it implements are sound for that theory. This is an argument about the theory, not a proof about the code: it is tested, not verified."
msgstr "**终止性。** 由带 W 类型和直谓宇宙的 Martin-Löf 类型论的归一化定理，良类型项的求值会终止。检查器只对已经检查过的项求值（不变式 2），且 `type_inf` 与 `type_chk` 的每次递归调用都作用于真子项，因此只要它实现的规则对该理论可靠，检查器就在每个输入上终止。这是关于理论的论证，而不是关于代码的证明：它经过测试，未经验证。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:305
msgid "Known gaps"
msgstr "已知缺口"

#: manual/design/elab.md:307
msgid "The implementation is a work in progress, and some rules are weaker or stronger than the theory above. They are recorded here so that users can avoid them; the code is unchanged."
msgstr "本实现仍在开发中，部分规则比上述理论更弱或更强。在此记录它们，以便用户避开；代码保持不变。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:309
msgid "**Subtyping only for $\\Pi$, $\\Sigma$ and universes.** $W$ and identity types are compared by conversion, without cumulativity in their components."
msgstr "**只有 $\\Pi$、$\\Sigma$ 和宇宙有子类型。** $W$ 和恒等类型按转换比较，其分量上没有累积性。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:310
msgid "**No $\\eta$ below identity and W values.** The type-directed conversion $\\equiv_A$ uses $\\eta$ at $\\Pi$, $\\Sigma$ and $\\mathbf 1$ only. At an identity type, a W type or a neutral type it compares read-backs, so the components of $\\mathrm{refl}$, $\\sup$ and stuck eliminations are compared without $\\eta$. For a variable $f : \\mathbf 1 \\to \\mathbf 1$ the checker accepts $\\mathrm{refl}\\;f : \\mathrm{Id}(\\mathbf 1 \\to \\mathbf 1, f, \\lambda x.\\,f\\,x)$, but rejects $\\mathrm{refl}\\,(\\mathrm{refl}\\;f) : \\mathrm{Id}\\bigl(\\mathrm{Id}(\\mathbf 1 \\to \\mathbf 1, f, f), \\mathrm{refl}\\;f, \\mathrm{refl}\\,(\\lambda x.\\,f\\,x)\\bigr)$ with `Rfl endpoints mismatch`, although the endpoints are definitionally equal. The checker is incomplete here, not unsound."
msgstr "**身份类型与 W 值之下没有 $\\eta$。** 类型导向的转换 $\\equiv_A$ 只在 $\\Pi$、$\\Sigma$ 和 $\\mathbf 1$ 处使用 $\\eta$。在身份类型、W 类型或中性类型处它比较读回结果，因此 $\\mathrm{refl}$、$\\sup$ 以及卡住的消去的分量在比较时不使用 $\\eta$。对变量 $f : \\mathbf 1 \\to \\mathbf 1$，检查器接受 $\\mathrm{refl}\\;f : \\mathrm{Id}(\\mathbf 1 \\to \\mathbf 1, f, \\lambda x.\\,f\\,x)$，却以 `Rfl endpoints mismatch` 拒绝 $\\mathrm{refl}\\,(\\mathrm{refl}\\;f) : \\mathrm{Id}\\bigl(\\mathrm{Id}(\\mathbf 1 \\to \\mathbf 1, f, f), \\mathrm{refl}\\;f, \\mathrm{refl}\\,(\\lambda x.\\,f\\,x)\\bigr)$，尽管两个端点定义相等。检查器在这里是不完备的，而非不可靠。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:311
msgid "**Open terms at the top level abort.** $(\\textsf{Var})$ looks up $\\rho(i)$ without a bounds check, so `type_inf_0(ctx, Bound(0))` panics instead of raising `TypeError`."
msgstr "**顶层的开项会中止。** $(\\textsf{Var})$ 查找 $\\rho(i)$ 时没有边界检查，因此 `type_inf_0(ctx, Bound(0))` 会 panic，而不是引发 `TypeError`。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:313
msgid "Alternatives rejected"
msgstr "被否决的方案"

#: manual/design/elab.md:315
msgid "**Typed terms with names.** Named variables need capture-avoiding substitution and make $\\alpha$-equivalence a separate check; de Bruijn indices avoid both."
msgstr "**带名字的类型化项。** 具名变量需要避免捕获的代换，并使 $\\alpha$-等价成为单独的检查；德布鲁因索引避免了这两者。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:316
msgid "**Substitution-based normalisation.** Repeated syntactic substitution is slower and harder to get right than evaluation into closures, and it still needs a separate conversion check."
msgstr "**基于代换的归一化。** 反复的语法代换比求值到闭包更慢、更难写对，而且仍需要单独的转换检查。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:317
msgid "**Impredicative or self-containing universes.** $\\mathcal U : \\mathcal U$ is inconsistent, and an impredicative $\\mathrm{Prop}$ is not part of the theory stella follows."
msgstr "**非直谓或包含自身的宇宙。** $\\mathcal U : \\mathcal U$ 是不一致的，而非直谓的 $\\mathrm{Prop}$ 不属于 stella 所遵循的理论。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:318
msgid "**Inductive families.** W types provide well-founded trees with a single eliminator, which keeps the kernel small; general inductive definitions would need a positivity checker."
msgstr "**归纳族。** W 类型以单一消去子提供良基树，使内核保持精简；一般的归纳定义需要正性检查器。"

#: manual/design/elab.md:320
msgid "Boundaries"
msgstr "边界"

#: manual/design/elab.md:322
msgid "The package deliberately does not:"
msgstr "本包有意不做以下事情："

#: manual/design/elab.md:324
msgid "parse a surface syntax, elaborate implicit arguments or solve unification problems; terms are built as MoonBit values in core syntax;"
msgstr "解析表层语法、细化隐式参数或求解合一问题；项以核心语法的 MoonBit 值构建；"

#: manual/design/elab.md:325
msgid "support definitions, `let` or global definitions with bodies; the context holds postulates (names with types) only;"
msgstr "支持定义、`let` 或带定义体的全局定义；上下文只包含公设（带类型的名字）；"

#: manual/design/elab.md:326
msgid "provide universe polymorphism, inductive families, an empty type or sum types;"
msgstr "提供宇宙多态、归纳族、空类型或和类型；"

#: manual/design/elab.md:327
msgid "implement univalence, higher inductive types or any other feature of homotopy type theory, although the treatise describes them as goals of the project;"
msgstr "实现单价性、高阶归纳类型或同伦类型论的任何其他特性，尽管论著将它们描述为项目的目标；"

#: manual/design/elab.md:328
msgid "guarantee anything for ill-typed input to the evaluator; `eval_inf`, `eval_chk` and the `val_` functions may panic."
msgstr "对求值器的类型错误输入作任何保证；`eval_inf`、`eval_chk` 和 `val_` 函数可能 panic。"

#: manual/index.md:1
msgid "stella"
msgstr "stella"

#: manual/index.md:3
msgid "This manual documents the intended `v0.2.0` release of `Luna-Flow/stella`, the current `main` branch."
msgstr "本手册记录 `Luna-Flow/stella` 预定的 `v0.2.0` 版本，即当前的 `main` 分支。"

#: manual/index.md:5
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "概览"

#: manual/index.md:7
msgid "stella is a proof assistant written in MoonBit and still a work in progress. Its kernel is the `elab` package: the core syntax of a Martin-Löf type theory, evaluation into values, read-back into normal forms, and a bidirectional type checker whose definitional equality is decided by normalisation by evaluation."
msgstr "stella 是一个用 MoonBit 编写、仍在开发中的证明助手。其内核是 `elab` 包：包含 Martin-Löf 类型论的核心语法、求值为值、读回为范式，以及一个双向类型检查器，其定义等价由求值归一化判定。"

#: manual/index.md:9
msgid "The type theory has the unit type, $\\Pi$ types, $\\Sigma$ types, identity types with the $J$ eliminator, W types with recursion, and a cumulative hierarchy of predicative universes, with subtyping that is contravariant in the domain of $\\Pi$ types."
msgstr "该类型论包含单位类型、$\\Pi$ 类型、$\\Sigma$ 类型、带 $J$ 消去子的恒等类型、带递归的 W 类型，以及直谓宇宙的累积层级，其子类型关系在 $\\Pi$ 类型的定义域上逆变。"

#: manual/index.md:11
msgid "The release candidate centers on these changes:"
msgstr "本候选版本的核心变化如下："

#: manual/index.md:13
msgid "The kernel types derive `Debug` instead of `Show`: print them with `debug_inspect`, `Repr(x)` or `@debug.to_string(x)`."
msgstr "内核类型派生 `Debug` 而不是 `Show`：请用 `debug_inspect`、`Repr(x)` 或 `@debug.to_string(x)` 打印它们。"

#: manual/index.md:14
msgid "The $J$ eliminator checks the domains of its motive, and `WRec` checks the domains of its family and motive by subtyping."
msgstr "$J$ 消去子检查其动机的定义域，`WRec` 通过子类型检查其族与动机的定义域。"

#: manual/index.md:15
msgid "`Rfl` compares its endpoints by conversion with $\\eta$, `def_eq` is reflexive on neutral applications, and a stuck `wrec` reads back to a term that evaluates to itself."
msgstr "`Rfl` 用带 $\\eta$ 的转换比较其端点，`def_eq` 在中性应用上是自反的，卡住的 `wrec` 读回为一个求值后等于自身的项。"

#: manual/index.md:17
msgid "Install"
msgstr "安装"

#: manual/index.md:23
msgid "Then import `\"Luna-Flow/stella/elab\"` and `\"moonbitlang/core/list\"`, which provides contexts and environments, in your `moon.pkg`. The package needs the MoonBit toolchain 0.10 or later (`moonc` ≥ 0.10) and has no dependencies besides the MoonBit core library."
msgstr "然后在你的 `moon.pkg` 中导入 `\"Luna-Flow/stella/elab\"` 和提供上下文与环境的 `\"moonbitlang/core/list\"`。本包需要 MoonBit 工具链 0.10 或更高版本（`moonc` ≥ 0.10），除 MoonBit 核心库外没有其他依赖。"

#: manual/index.md:25
msgid "[!NOTE] `moon.mod` still declares `0.1.2`, the last published version. That version implements `Show` for the kernel types and lacks the fixes listed in the [changelog](../../CHANGELOG.md); the pages below describe `main`."
msgstr "[!NOTE] `moon.mod` 仍声明 `0.1.2`，即最后发布的版本。该版本为内核类型实现了 `Show`，并且缺少[变更日志](../../CHANGELOG.md)中列出的修复；以下页面描述的是 `main`。"

